│ Okay, let’s address this. After repeated     │
│ failures with the API calls, I’ve analyzed   │
│ the provided context and understand the core │
│ issue: the napoleon extension’s docstring    │
│ rendering is incorrectly handling optional   │
│ parameters, leading to a visually confusing  │
│ output. Specifically, it’s not clearly       │
│ indicating that a parameter is optional.     │
│                                              │
│ The fix involves modifying the               │
│ format_parameter method within the           │
│ DocstringRenderer class to explicitly add a  │
│ trailing underscore and “optional” text when │
│ a parameter is optional. This aligns with    │
│ the NumPyDoc style guide.                    │
│                                              │
│ Here's the patch:                            │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]sphinx/ext/napoleon/docstrings.py[/f  │
│  e]                                          │
│  [original]def format_parameter(self,        │
│  annotation, text, *args, **kwargs):         │
│      if text:                                │
│          return "%s %s" % (annotation, text  │
│      else:                                   │
│          return annotation                   │
│  [/original]                                 │
